ISSUES
- [4] partial rebuild does not propagate front matter changes to dependent pages/feed
  - problem: when a markdown file changes, rebuild_md() only re-renders that page.
  - impact: pages that render collections (sections/tags) and RSS feed can become stale after front matter edits (title/date/section/tags/url).
  - expected: markdown edits should also refresh dependent collection pages and feed (or trigger full rebuild when needed).
  - actual: dependent outputs stay outdated until the next full build.
  - proposed fix: in watcher flow, compare old vs new front matter for changed .md files; if metadata changed (or file create/delete/move), run full build; otherwise keep partial rebuild.

PAST ISSUES
- [5] markdown output vs static file collision is not detected
  - problem: if a markdown file compiles to a path already copied from static/, build succeeds and markdown silently overwrites static output.
  - repro examples:
    - static/post.html + content/post.md
    - static/blog/index.html + content/blog/index.md
    - static/index.html + content/index.md
  - expected: fail build with explicit collision error (same policy as content raw html vs markdown collisions).
  - actual: build succeeds; resulting file is markdown output.
  - notes: direct raw collision static/post.html + content/post.html already raises (target exists check). gap is specifically markdown output overwriting files previously copied from static/.

